        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 140 adds support for the <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-highlight-api-1/#dom-highlightregistry-highlightsfrompoint\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">HighlightRegisty.highlightsFromPoint()</code></a> method; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/4552801607483392\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/4552801607483392</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've tested it in Chrome 140, and it works fine; Chrome 139 throws <code class=\"notranslate\">Uncaught TypeError: CSS.highlights.highlightsFromPoint is not a function</code>.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
